11. Resource Management Approaches
Two ways to manage resources:
1️⃣ Imperative
You tell the cluster what action to perform.
Example:
oc create deployment my-app --image example.com/my-image
Add environment variable:
oc set env deployment/my-app TEAM=red
Create pod:
oc run example-pod \
--image=registry.access.redhat.com/ubi8/httpd-24 \
--env GREETING="Hello" \
--port 8080
Imperative is fast for testing.
________________________________________
2️⃣ Declarative
You define desired state in YAML.
Example:
oc create -f deployment.yaml
Cluster ensures the state matches the YAML.
Best for:
•	version control
•	automation
•	CI/CD
________________________________________
12. oc new-app Command
new-app automatically creates resources.
Example using image:
oc new-app --image example.com/my-app:dev
Example using Git repo:
oc new-app https://github.com/apache/httpd.git
Example using template:
oc new-app --template mysql-persistent
It automatically creates:
•	ImageStream
•	Deployment
•	Service
